{% set page_title = "Spain 29N polls · average, range and limits" %}
{% set page_desc = "Aggregated average of published polls for Spain's 29 November 2026 general election, with range, sources and limits. Not a forecast." %}
{% set canonical = site_url ~ "/en.html" %}
{% set page_lang = "en" %}
{% set page_alt_es = site_url ~ "/" %}
{% set page_alt_en = canonical %}
{% set jsonld = webpages['en.html'] %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
{% include "_head.html.j2" %}
</head>
<body>
{% include "_en_nav.html.j2" %}

<main class="container">
  <h1 style="margin:18px 0 4px;font-size:34px;letter-spacing:-0.03em">Spain 29N: polls, range and limits</h1>
  <p class="muted" style="margin:0 0 16px">An English guide to the <strong>29N</strong> observatory. The full interactive site and source notes are in Spanish; this section explains the data, the method and what it does not say.</p>

  <div class="hero-kpis">
    <div class="hk"><b>{{ n_polls }}</b><span>polls in the average</span></div>
    <div class="hk"><b>{{ health.n_pollsters or "—" }}</b><span>polling houses</span></div>
    <div class="hk"><b>{{ days_to_election }}</b><span>days to election day</span></div>
    <div class="hk"><b>{{ days_to_blackout }}</b><span>days to polling blackout</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="stamp">Updated: <strong>{{ updated_at }}</strong> · last poll: <strong>{{ last_poll_date or "—" }}</strong> · sample declared in {{ health.sample_pct or 0 }}% of polls.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="cardhead"><h2>Current average</h2><span class="hint">range = observed polls, not a confidence interval</span></div>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Party</th><th>Average</th><th>Range</th><th>Median</th><th>Polls</th><th>Houses</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for p in parties_table[:7] %}
          <tr>
            <td><strong>{{ p.party }}</strong></td>
            <td class="num">{{ fmt_pct(p.mean) }}%</td>
            <td class="num">{{ fmt_pct(p.min) }}–{{ fmt_pct(p.max) }}</td>
            <td class="num">{{ fmt_pct(p.median) }}%</td>
            <td class="num">{{ p.n }}</td>
            <td class="num">{% if p.n_houses_window %}{{ p.n_houses_window }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="muted small">The average combines published polls with <strong>recency</strong> and <strong>declared sample size</strong> when available. The range is descriptive: not a confidence interval, not a prediction.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="cardhead"><h2>Read next</h2></div>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li><a href="/en/method.html"><strong>Method</strong></a> — how the average, weights and house contrast are built.</li>
      <li><a href="/en/hemicycle.html"><strong>Hemicycle</strong></a> — the 350-seat mechanical simulation, with its limits.</li>
      <li><a href="/en/robustness.html"><strong>Robustness</strong></a> — sample, dispersion, source and house concentration.</li>
      <li><a href="/en/limits.html"><strong>Limits and glossary</strong></a> — what the observatory does not say, and the key terms.</li>
      <li><a href="/en/data.html"><strong>Data</strong></a> — JSON, versioned files, hashes and reproducibility.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="cardhead"><h2>What this is not</h2></div>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li><strong>Not a forecast.</strong> It does not estimate the election result or the next government.</li>
      <li><strong>Not a single poll.</strong> It is a weighted average of polls published in the last 14 days.</li>
      <li><strong>Not demographically corrected.</strong> The site does not model age, sex, income or territory.</li>
      <li><strong>Not the full Congress.</strong> The hemicycle is a national D'Hondt simulation, not the real provincial allocation.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</main>

{% include "_en_footer.html.j2" %}
</body>
</html>
